# Run outputs and generated figures live outside the repo.
#
# What makes a result reproducible is the config, the seed and the code version, and
# all three are tracked here. The JSONs are outputs: 1174 files and 92 MB of them,
# in nineteen top-level directories, which is noise for anyone who arrives wanting to
# use the tool. The numbers the paper cites live in its own repo as generated macros.
#
# Set PHOTOSVI_RUNS to choose where they go; the runner scripts default to
# $PHOTOSVI_RUNS.
runs/
runs_*/
outputs/
diagnostics/
logs/

# pytest-cov artefact
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
photosvi_toy/
